/-!
# Hamiltonian diffeotopies and the Hamiltonian group

Let `σ` be a two-form on a manifold `M`, for instance a symplectic form, and let `φ_t`,
`t ∈ [0, 1]`, be a smooth diffeotopy of `M` with motion `Φ (x, t) = φ_t x` and velocity field
`X_t = (∂ₜ φ_t) ∘ φ_t⁻¹`. With the convention `ι_{X_f} σ = df`, the diffeotopy is generated by a
time-dependent Hamiltonian `H_t` when `ι_{X_t} σ = dH_t` for all `t`. Pulled back along `φ_t`
this reads

`σ_{φ_t x}(∂ₜ φ_t x, dφ_t v) = d(F_t)_x(v)` for `F_t = H_t ∘ φ_t`,

an identity between the pullback `Φ^* σ` of `σ` to the cylinder `M × [0, 1]`, contracted with
`∂ₜ`, and the spatial derivative of a smooth function `F` on the cylinder. A function `F` with
this property is a **Hamiltonian of `φ_t` read along the motion**
(`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian`). Working with `F` rather than with `H` avoids the inverse
maps `φ_t⁻¹`, and the left-hand side is exactly the integrand of the flux form
(`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.fluxForm`).

A diffeotopy is **Hamiltonian** (`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsHamiltonian`) when every `φ_t` preserves
`σ` and it has such a Hamiltonian. These are the smooth Hamiltonian isotopies of `(M, σ)`. The
Hamiltonians compose as expected (`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian.trans`,
`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian.symm`, `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian.transDiffeomorph`):
if every `ψ_t` preserves `σ`, then for the pointwise composite `ψ_t ∘ φ_t` the function
`(x, t) ↦ G (φ_t x, t) + F (x, t)` is a Hamiltonian; if every `φ_t` preserves `σ`, then for the
inverse `φ_t⁻¹` the function `(x, t) ↦ -F (φ_t⁻¹ x, t)` is one; and for the conjugate
`f ∘ φ_t ∘ f⁻¹` by a diffeomorphism `f` the function `(y, t) ↦ F (f⁻¹ y, t)` is one for the form
`σ` when `F` is a Hamiltonian for `f^* σ`. The flow of a complete Hamiltonian vector field `X_f`
of a smooth function `f`, run for duration `a`, is Hamiltonian with Hamiltonian
`(x, t) ↦ a f(x)` (`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.hasHamiltonian_globalFlowDiffeotopy`).

The flux form of a diffeotopy with a Hamiltonian `F` is the exterior derivative of a smooth
function vanishing wherever `F (x, ·) = 0`, constructed as `x ↦ ∫₀¹ F (x, t) dt`
(`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian.exists_fluxForm_eq_mextDerivₗ`), so it is exact
(`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian.fluxForm_mem_exactForms`) and Hamiltonian isotopies have zero
flux (`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsHamiltonian.flux_eq_zero`).

The **Hamiltonian group** `Ham(M, σ)` (`TauCeti.SmoothForm.hamiltonianGroup`) is the group of
final diffeomorphisms of Hamiltonian diffeotopies. It is a subgroup of the isotopy stabilizer
`G_σ` of `σ`, normal in the group of all diffeomorphisms preserving `σ`, and for a closed `σ` it
lies in the kernel of the endpoint flux `G_σ → H¹_dR(M) / Γ_σ`
(`TauCeti.hamiltonianGroup_subgroupOf_le_ker_endpointFlux`).

As for `TauCeti.SmoothForm.isotopyStabilizer`, the diffeotopies here are not required to be
constant near the ends of the time interval, and a Hamiltonian is not normalized: it is
determined by the diffeotopy up to adding a smooth function of time alone on each connected
component of `M`, which changes neither the diffeotopy nor its flux.

## Implementation notes

The flux integrand of a diffeotopy with Hamiltonian `F` is the contraction of `-d(F dt)` with
`∂ₜ` on spatial vectors, where `t` is the time coordinate of the cylinder. The one-form `F dt`
vanishes on both ends of the cylinder, so the cochain-homotopy identity of the homotopy operator
(`TauCeti.homotopyOperator_mextDeriv_of_mpullback_eq_zero`) identifies the flux form with
`d (∫₀¹ F dt)`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian σ Φ F`: `F` is a Hamiltonian of the diffeotopy `Φ` for `σ`,
  read along the motion.
* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsHamiltonian σ Φ`: `Φ` is a Hamiltonian diffeotopy of `σ`.
* `TauCeti.SmoothForm.hamiltonianGroup σ`: the Hamiltonian group `Ham(M, σ)`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian.exists_fluxForm_eq_mextDerivₗ`: the flux form of a
  diffeotopy with Hamiltonian `F` is `d g` for a smooth function `g` vanishing wherever
  `F (x, ·) = 0`.
* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian.fluxForm_mem_exactForms`,
  `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsHamiltonian.flux_eq_zero`: Hamiltonian diffeotopies have exact flux form
  and zero flux.
* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian.trans`, `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian.symm`,
  `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian.transDiffeomorph`: Hamiltonians of composites, inverses
  and conjugates.
* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.isHamiltonian_globalFlowDiffeotopy`: complete autonomous Hamiltonian flows
  are Hamiltonian diffeotopies.
* `TauCeti.SmoothForm.hamiltonianGroup_le_isotopyStabilizer`,
  `TauCeti.SmoothForm.mul_mul_inv_mem_hamiltonianGroup`: `Ham(M, σ)` lies in `G_σ` and is normal
  in the group of diffeomorphisms preserving `σ`.
* `TauCeti.hamiltonianGroup_subgroupOf_le_ker_endpointFlux`: Hamiltonian diffeomorphisms have
  trivial endpoint flux.

## References

* Dusa McDuff and Dietmar Salamon, *Introduction to Symplectic Topology*, 3rd ed., Oxford
  University Press, 2017, Sections 3.1 and 10.2 (Hamiltonian isotopies, the group of
  Hamiltonian symplectomorphisms and the flux homomorphism).
* Augustin Banyaga, *The Structure of Classical Diffeomorphism Groups*, Kluwer, 1997,
  Chapter 3.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open Set
open scoped ContDiff Manifold

namespace TauCeti

namespace Diffeotopy

variable {E H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace H]
  {J : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H} {M : Type*} [TopologicalSpace M] [ChartedSpace H M]
  [IsManifold J ∞ M]

/-- A smooth function `F` on the cylinder `M × [0, 1]` is a **Hamiltonian** of the diffeotopy
`φ_t` for the two-form `σ`, read along the motion, when the pullback `Φ^* σ` of `σ` along the
motion `Φ (x, t) = φ_t x` satisfies

`(Φ^* σ)_(x, t)(∂ₜ, v) = σ_{φ_t x}(∂ₜ φ_t x, dφ_t v) = d(F_t)_x(v)`

for every `(x, t)` and every tangent vector `v` at `x`. In terms of the velocity field
`X_t = (∂ₜ φ_t) ∘ φ_t⁻¹` and of `H_t = F_t ∘ φ_t⁻¹`, this says `φ_t^* (ι_{X_t} σ) = φ_t^* dH_t`,
that is `ι_{X_t} σ = dH_t`: the diffeotopy is generated by the time-dependent Hamiltonian `H`, with
the convention `ι_{X_f} σ = df`. -/
def HasHamiltonian (σ : SmoothForm J M ℝ 2) (Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M)
    (F : M × unitInterval → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ F ∧
    ∀ (p : M × unitInterval) (v : E),
      mpullback (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) J Φ.cylinderMap σ.val p
          ![((0 : E), (1 : TangentSpace (𝓡∂ 1) p.2)), (v, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))] =
        mvfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) F p (v, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))

variable {σ : SmoothForm J M ℝ 2} {Φ Ψ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M} {F G : M × unitInterval → ℝ}

/-- Unfolding `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian`: `F` is smooth and satisfies
`σ_{φ_t x}(∂ₜ φ_t x, dφ_t v) = d(F_t)_x(v)`. -/
theorem hasHamiltonian_iff : Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F ↔
    ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ F ∧
      ∀ (p : M × unitInterval) (v : E),
        mpullback (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) J Φ.cylinderMap σ.val p
            ![((0 : E), (1 : TangentSpace (𝓡∂ 1) p.2)), (v, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))] =
          mvfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) F p (v, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1))) :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- A Hamiltonian of a diffeotopy is smooth. -/
theorem HasHamiltonian.contMDiff (h : Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F) :
    ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ F :=
  h.1

/-- The defining identity of a Hamiltonian `F` of `φ_t`, read along the motion:
`σ_{φ_t x}(∂ₜ φ_t x, dφ_t v) = d(F_t)_x(v)`. -/
theorem HasHamiltonian.mpullback_cylinderMap_apply (h : Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F)
    (p : M × unitInterval) (v : E) :
    mpullback (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) J Φ.cylinderMap σ.val p
        ![((0 : E), (1 : TangentSpace (𝓡∂ 1) p.2)), (v, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))] =
      mvfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) F p (v, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1))) :=
  h.2 p v

/-! ### The flux form of a Hamiltonian diffeotopy -/

/-- The time coordinate `(x, t) ↦ t` of the cylinder, as a real function. -/
private def timeCoord : M × unitInterval → ℝ := fun p ↦ (p.2 : ℝ)

omit [IsManifold J ∞ M] in
private theorem contMDiff_timeCoord :
    ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ (timeCoord : M × unitInterval → ℝ) :=
  contMDiff_subtypeVal_Icc.comp contMDiff_snd

omit [IsManifold J ∞ M] in
/-- The derivative of the time coordinate only sees the time component of a tangent vector. -/
private theorem mvfderiv_timeCoord (p : M × unitInterval)
    (v : TangentSpace (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) p) :
    mvfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) (timeCoord : M × unitInterval → ℝ) p v =
      mvfderiv (𝓡∂ 1) (Subtype.val : unitInterval → ℝ) p.2 v.2 :=
  mvfderiv_comp_snd_apply Subtype.val p v

variable (J) in
/-- The one-form `F dt` on the cylinder, where `t` is the time coordinate. -/
private def smulTimeForm (F : M × unitInterval → ℝ) :
    RoughForm (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) (M × unitInterval) ℝ 1 :=
  fun p ↦ F p • mextDeriv (RoughForm.ofFunction (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) timeCoord) p

private theorem isSmoothForm_mextDeriv_timeCoord :
    IsSmoothForm (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) ∞
      (mextDeriv (RoughForm.ofFunction (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) (timeCoord : M × unitInterval → ℝ))) :=
  isSmoothForm_mextDeriv (isSmoothForm_ofFunction_iff.2 contMDiff_timeCoord) (by simp)

private theorem isSmoothForm_smulTimeForm (hF : ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ F) :
    IsSmoothForm (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) ∞ (smulTimeForm J F) :=
  (isSmoothForm_mextDeriv_timeCoord (J := J) (M := M)).fun_smul hF

omit [IsManifold J ∞ M] in
/-- The one-form `F dt` restricts to zero on every time slice `M × {c}` of the cylinder. -/
private theorem mpullback_smulTimeForm_eq_zero (F : M × unitInterval → ℝ) (c : unitInterval) :
    mpullback J (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) (fun x ↦ (x, c)) (smulTimeForm J F) = 0 := by
  funext x
  ext v
  rw [mpullback_apply, smulTimeForm, ContinuousAlternatingMap.smul_apply, mextDeriv_ofFunction,
    ContinuousAlternatingMap.ofSubsingleton_apply_apply, mvfderiv_timeCoord, mfderiv_prod_left]
  exact (congrArg (F (x, c) • ·) (map_zero (mvfderiv (𝓡∂ 1)
    (Subtype.val : unitInterval → ℝ) c))).trans (mul_zero (F (x, c)))

/-- The exterior derivative of `F dt` is `dF ∧ dt`. -/
private theorem mextDeriv_smulTimeForm_apply (hF : ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ F)
    (p : M × unitInterval) (u w : TangentSpace (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) p) :
    mextDeriv (smulTimeForm J F) p ![u, w] =
      mvfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) F p u *
          mvfderiv (𝓡∂ 1) (Subtype.val : unitInterval → ℝ) p.2 w.2 -
        mvfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) F p w *
          mvfderiv (𝓡∂ 1) (Subtype.val : unitInterval → ℝ) p.2 u.2 := by
  unfold smulTimeForm
  rw [mextDeriv_fun_smul_apply (hF.mdifferentiableAt (by simp))
    (isSmoothForm_mextDeriv_timeCoord.contMDiff.mdifferentiableAt (by simp)),
    mextDeriv_mextDeriv_ofFunction (contMDiff_timeCoord.of_le (by simp))]
  simp only [mextDeriv_ofFunction, ContinuousAlternatingMap.ofSubsingleton_apply_apply,
    Matrix.cons_val_zero, mvfderiv_timeCoord, Pi.zero_apply, ContinuousAlternatingMap.coe_zero,
    mul_zero, add_zero]

/-- **The flux form of a Hamiltonian diffeotopy.** If `φ_t` has a Hamiltonian `F` for `σ`, read
along the motion, then the flux form of `φ_t` is `d g` for some smooth function `g` vanishing
at every point `x` with `F (x, t) = 0` for all `t`. The proof takes `g x = ∫₀¹ F (x, t) dt`.
Neither closedness nor nondegeneracy of `σ` is needed. -/
theorem HasHamiltonian.exists_fluxForm_eq_mextDerivₗ (h : Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F) :
    ∃ g : SmoothForm J M ℝ 0, (∀ x, (∀ t, F (x, t) = 0) → g.val x = 0) ∧
      Φ.fluxForm σ = mextDerivₗ J 0 g := by
  have : IsManifold J ((⊤ : ℕ∞) + 1 : WithTop ℕ∞) M := IsManifold.of_le (n := ∞) (by simp)
  have hβ := isSmoothForm_smulTimeForm h.1
  -- `h (d (F dt)) = -d (h (F dt))`, because `F dt` vanishes on both ends of the cylinder.
  have key := homotopyOperator_mextDeriv_of_mpullback_eq_zero (hβ.of_le (by simp))
    (mpullback_smulTimeForm_eq_zero F 0) (mpullback_smulTimeForm_eq_zero F 1)
  refine ⟨⟨homotopyOperator (smulTimeForm J F),
    (IsSmoothForm.homotopyOperator hβ).mem_smoothBundleForms⟩, fun x hx ↦ ?_,
    (Subtype.ext ?_).symm⟩
  · -- Over such a point the one-form `F dt` vanishes at every time.
    refine homotopyOperator_apply_eq_zero fun t v ↦ ?_
    rw [smulTimeForm, hx t, zero_smul, ContinuousAlternatingMap.coe_zero, Pi.zero_apply]
  rw [mextDerivₗ_apply, coe_fluxForm, ← neg_eq_iff_eq_neg.mpr key,
    ← neg_one_smul ℝ (homotopyOperator (mextDeriv (smulTimeForm J F))), ← homotopyOperator_smul]
  -- The integrands of the two homotopy operators agree: both are `dF` on spatial vectors.
  funext x
  rw [homotopyOperator_apply, homotopyOperator_apply]
  refine intervalIntegral.integral_congr (E := E [⋀^Fin 1]→L[ℝ] ℝ) fun t _ ↦
    ContinuousAlternatingMap.ext fun v ↦ ?_
  set p : M × unitInterval := (x, projIcc 0 1 zero_le_one t)
  set u : TangentSpace (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) p := ((0 : E), (1 : TangentSpace (𝓡∂ 1) p.2))
  set w : TangentSpace (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) p := (v 0, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))
  have hv : (Matrix.vecCons u (ContinuousLinearMap.inl ℝ E (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)) ∘ v) :
      Fin 2 → TangentSpace (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) p) = ![u, w] :=
    -- Each entry unfolds `Matrix.vecCons` and `ContinuousLinearMap.inl`; the simp lemmas for these
    -- leave goals whose sides differ only by unfolding `TangentSpace` of the product.
    funext fun i ↦ by fin_cases i <;> rfl
  have hu : mvfderiv (𝓡∂ 1) (Subtype.val : unitInterval → ℝ) p.2 u.2 = 1 :=
    mfderiv_subtypeVal_Icc_one p.2
  have h1 : mextDeriv (smulTimeForm J F) p ![u, w] = -mvfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) F p w := by
    have hw : mvfderiv (𝓡∂ 1) (Subtype.val : unitInterval → ℝ) p.2 w.2 = 0 := map_zero _
    rw [mextDeriv_smulTimeForm_apply h.1, hu, hw, mul_zero, zero_sub, mul_one]
  have h2 : (SmoothForm.mpullback Φ.cylinderMap Φ.contMDiff_cylinderMap σ).val p ![u, w] =
      mvfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) F p w := by
    rw [SmoothForm.coe_mpullback]
    exact h.2 p (v 0)
  simp only [ContinuousAlternatingMap.compContinuousLinearMap_apply, Pi.smul_apply, neg_one_smul]
  -- Both sides evaluate the forms on `vecCons ∂ₜ (inl ∘ v)`; currying unfolds definitionally.
  exact (congrArg Neg.neg ((congrArg (mextDeriv (smulTimeForm J F) p) hv).trans h1)).trans
    ((neg_neg _).trans (h2.symm.trans (congrArg _ hv.symm)))

/-- **The flux form of a Hamiltonian diffeotopy is exact.** If `φ_t` has a Hamiltonian `F` for
`σ`, read along the motion, then the flux form of `φ_t` is exact. Neither closedness nor
nondegeneracy of `σ` is needed. -/
theorem HasHamiltonian.fluxForm_mem_exactForms (h : Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F) :
    Φ.fluxForm σ ∈ exactForms J M 1 := by
  obtain ⟨g, -, hg⟩ := h.exists_fluxForm_eq_mextDerivₗ
  rw [exactForms_succ]
  exact ⟨g, hg.symm⟩

/-- **The flux of a Hamiltonian diffeotopy vanishes.** -/
theorem HasHamiltonian.flux_eq_zero {σ : closedForms J M 2} (h : Φ.HasHamiltonian σ.val F)
    (hΦ : Φ.final ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ.val) : Φ.flux σ hΦ = 0 := by
  rw [flux_def, deRhamCohomology.mk_eq_zero_iff]
  exact h.fluxForm_mem_exactForms

/-! ### Composition, inversion and conjugation -/

omit [IsManifold J ∞ M] in
/-- By the chain rule, the derivative of `(x, t) ↦ G (φ_t x, t)` along a spatial vector `(v, 0)`
at `p` is the derivative of `G` along `(dφ_t v, 0)` at `(φ_t x, t)`. -/
private theorem mvfderiv_comp_cylinderMap_prodMk_snd_space
    (hG : ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ G) (p : M × unitInterval) (v : E) :
    mvfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) (fun q ↦ G (Φ.cylinderMap q, q.2)) p
        (v, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1))) =
      mvfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) G (Φ.cylinderMap p, p.2)
        (mfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) J Φ.cylinderMap p (v, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1))),
          (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1))) :=
  (mvfderiv_comp_apply p (hG.mdifferentiableAt (by simp))
    (Φ.contMDiff_cylinderMap_prodMk_snd.mdifferentiableAt (by simp)) _).trans
    (congrArg _ (Φ.mfderiv_cylinderMap_prodMk_snd (by simp) p _))

/-- If every map `ψ_t` preserves `σ`, the pullback of `σ` along the motion of `ψ` restricts on each
time slice `M × {t}` to `σ`. -/
private theorem mpullback_cylinderMap_apply_space
    (hΨ : ∀ t, Ψ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) (q : M × unitInterval)
    (a b : TangentSpace J q.1) :
    mpullback (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) J Ψ.cylinderMap σ.val q
        ![(a, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1))), (b, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))] =
      σ.val q.1 ![a, b] := by
  have hs : MDifferentiable J (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) fun z : M ↦ (z, q.2) :=
    (contMDiff_id.prodMk contMDiff_const).mdifferentiable (n := 1) one_ne_zero
  have hslice : Ψ.cylinderMap ∘ (fun z ↦ (z, q.2)) = Ψ.timeSlice q.2 :=
    funext fun z ↦ by rw [Function.comp_apply, cylinderMap_apply, timeSlice_apply]
  rw [← (SmoothForm.mem_diffeomorphStabilizer_iff_forall.1 (hΨ q.2)) q.1, ← hslice,
    mpullback_comp hs (Ψ.contMDiff_cylinderMap.mdifferentiable (by simp))]
  simp only [mpullback_apply]
  refine congrArg (σ.val (Ψ.cylinderMap q)) (funext fun i : Fin 2 ↦ ?_)
  refine congrArg (mfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) J Ψ.cylinderMap q) ?_
  rw [mfderiv_prod_left]
  -- `mfderiv_prod_left` gives `ContinuousLinearMap.inl` into
  -- `TangentSpace J q.1 × TangentSpace (𝓡∂ 1) q.2`, the tangent space of the product only up to
  -- unfolding `TangentSpace`, so `ContinuousLinearMap.inl_apply` does not rewrite. Each entry
  -- unfolds to `(a, 0)` or `(b, 0)`.
  fin_cases i <;> rfl

/-- **The flux integrand of a composite diffeotopy.** If every map `ψ_t` preserves `σ`, then
`(Ψ ∘ Φ)^* σ` evaluated on `∂ₜ` and a spatial vector `v` at `p = (x, t)` is `Ψ^* σ` evaluated on
`∂ₜ` and `dφ_t v` at `(φ_t x, t)`, plus `Φ^* σ` evaluated on `∂ₜ` and `v` at `p`. -/
private theorem mpullback_cylinderMap_trans_apply
    (hΨ : ∀ t, Ψ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) (p : M × unitInterval)
    (v : E) :
    mpullback (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) J (Φ.trans Ψ).cylinderMap σ.val p
        ![((0 : E), (1 : TangentSpace (𝓡∂ 1) p.2)), (v, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))] =
      mpullback (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) J Ψ.cylinderMap σ.val (Φ.cylinderMap p, p.2)
          ![((0 : E), (1 : TangentSpace (𝓡∂ 1) p.2)),
            (mfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) J Φ.cylinderMap p (v, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1))),
              (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))] +
        mpullback (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) J Φ.cylinderMap σ.val p
          ![((0 : E), (1 : TangentSpace (𝓡∂ 1) p.2)), (v, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))] := by
  set q : M × unitInterval := (Φ.cylinderMap p, p.2)
  set a : TangentSpace J q.1 :=
    mfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) J Φ.cylinderMap p ((0 : E), (1 : TangentSpace (𝓡∂ 1) p.2))
  set b : TangentSpace J q.1 :=
    mfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) J Φ.cylinderMap p (v, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))
  -- The motion of the composite is the motion of `ψ` after `(x, t) ↦ (φ_t x, t)`, which sends
  -- `∂ₜ` to `(a, ∂ₜ) = (0, ∂ₜ) + (a, 0)` and `(v, 0)` to `(b, 0)`.
  have hvec : (fun i ↦ mfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) (fun q ↦ (Φ.cylinderMap q, q.2)) p
      (![((0 : E), (1 : TangentSpace (𝓡∂ 1) p.2)), (v, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))] i)) =
      (![(((0 : E), (1 : TangentSpace (𝓡∂ 1) p.2)) : TangentSpace (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) q) +
          ((a, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1))) : TangentSpace (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) q),
        (b, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))] : Fin 2 → TangentSpace (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) q) := by
    funext i
    fin_cases i
    · exact (Φ.mfderiv_cylinderMap_prodMk_snd (by simp) p _).trans
        (Prod.ext (zero_add a).symm (add_zero _).symm)
    · exact Φ.mfderiv_cylinderMap_prodMk_snd (by simp) p _
  rw [cylinderMap_trans, mpullback_comp (Φ.contMDiff_cylinderMap_prodMk_snd.mdifferentiable
      (by simp)) (Ψ.contMDiff_cylinderMap.mdifferentiable (by simp)), mpullback_apply]
  refine ((congrArg (mpullback (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) J Ψ.cylinderMap σ.val q) hvec).trans
    ((mpullback (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) J Ψ.cylinderMap σ.val q).vecCons_add _ _ _)).trans
    (congrArg (_ + ·) ?_)
  -- Since `ψ_t` preserves `σ`, the purely spatial term is the integrand of `φ`.
  refine (mpullback_cylinderMap_apply_space hΨ q a b).trans ?_
  rw [mpullback_apply]
  -- The entries are the derivatives that `a` and `b` abbreviate.
  exact congrArg _ (funext fun i ↦ by fin_cases i <;> rfl)

/-- **Hamiltonians of a composite diffeotopy.** If `F` and `G` are Hamiltonians of `φ_t` and
`ψ_t`, read along their motions, and every `ψ_t` preserves `σ`, then
`(x, t) ↦ G (φ_t x, t) + F (x, t)` is a Hamiltonian of the composite `ψ_t ∘ φ_t`. In terms of the
time-dependent Hamiltonians `H_t = F_t ∘ φ_t⁻¹` and `K_t = G_t ∘ ψ_t⁻¹`, the composite is
generated by `K_t + H_t ∘ ψ_t⁻¹`. -/
theorem HasHamiltonian.trans (hF : Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F) (hG : Ψ.HasHamiltonian σ G)
    (hΨ : ∀ t, Ψ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) :
    (Φ.trans Ψ).HasHamiltonian σ (fun p ↦ G (Φ.cylinderMap p, p.2) + F p) := by
  have hL := Φ.contMDiff_cylinderMap_prodMk_snd
  refine ⟨(hG.1.comp hL).add hF.1, fun p v ↦ ?_⟩
  -- By the chain rule, `d (G ∘ L)` sends `(v, 0)` to `dG (dφ_t v, 0)`.
  have hGL := mvfderiv_comp_cylinderMap_prodMk_snd_space (Φ := Φ) hG.1 p v
  refine ((mpullback_cylinderMap_trans_apply hΨ p v).trans
    (congrArg₂ (· + ·) (hG.2 _ _) (hF.2 p v))).trans ?_
  exact (congrArg (· + _) hGL.symm).trans (DFunLike.congr_fun
    (mvfderiv_fun_add (g := fun q ↦ G (Φ.cylinderMap q, q.2)) (g' := F) (x := p)
      ((hG.1.comp hL).mdifferentiableAt (by simp)) (hF.1.mdifferentiableAt (by simp))) _).symm

/-- The constant diffeotopy has the zero Hamiltonian. -/
theorem hasHamiltonian_refl : (refl J ∞ M).HasHamiltonian σ 0 := by
  refine ⟨contMDiff_const, fun p v ↦ ?_⟩
  have hcyl : (refl J ∞ M).cylinderMap = Prod.fst := funext fun p ↦ by simp
  rw [hcyl, mpullback_apply, mfderiv_fst, mvfderiv_zero]
  -- The motion is stationary, so its time derivative vanishes.
  exact (σ.val p.1).map_coord_zero 0 rfl

/-- **Hamiltonians of the inverse diffeotopy.** If `F` is a Hamiltonian of `φ_t`, read along its
motion, and every `φ_t` preserves `σ`, then `(x, t) ↦ -F (φ_t⁻¹ x, t)` is a Hamiltonian of the
inverse diffeotopy `φ_t⁻¹`, which is generated by `-H_t ∘ φ_t` for `H_t = F_t ∘ φ_t⁻¹`. -/
theorem HasHamiltonian.symm (hF : Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F)
    (hΦ : ∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) :
    Φ.symm.HasHamiltonian σ (fun p ↦ -F (Φ.symm.cylinderMap p, p.2)) := by
  refine ⟨(hF.1.comp Φ.symm.contMDiff_cylinderMap_prodMk_snd).neg, fun p v ↦ ?_⟩
  -- The composite `φ_t ∘ φ_t⁻¹` is constant, so the two terms of its integrand cancel.
  have key := mpullback_cylinderMap_trans_apply (Φ := Φ.symm) hΦ p v
  rw [symm_trans_self] at key
  have hFL := mvfderiv_comp_cylinderMap_prodMk_snd_space (Φ := Φ.symm) hF.1 p v
  have h0 := ((hasHamiltonian_refl (σ := σ)).2 p v).trans
    (DFunLike.congr_fun (mvfderiv_zero (x := p)) _)
  have hsum := ((congrArg (· + _) (hF.2 _ _)).symm.trans key.symm).trans h0
  exact (neg_eq_of_add_eq_zero_right hsum).symm.trans ((congrArg Neg.neg hFL.symm).trans
    (DFunLike.congr_fun (mvfderiv_fun_neg (g := fun q ↦ F (Φ.symm.cylinderMap q, q.2)) (x := p))
      _).symm)

/-- **Naturality of Hamiltonians.** If `F` is a Hamiltonian of `φ_t` for the pullback `f^* σ` of
`σ` along a diffeomorphism `f : M → P`, then `(y, t) ↦ F (f⁻¹ y, t)` is a Hamiltonian of the
conjugated diffeotopy `f ∘ φ_t ∘ f⁻¹` for `σ`. -/
theorem HasHamiltonian.transDiffeomorph {P : Type*} [TopologicalSpace P] [ChartedSpace H P]
    [IsManifold J ∞ P] {σ : SmoothForm J P ℝ 2} (f : M ≃ₘ⟮J, J⟯ P)
    (hF : Φ.HasHamiltonian (SmoothForm.mpullback f f.contMDiff σ) F) :
    (Φ.transDiffeomorph f).HasHamiltonian σ (fun p ↦ F (f.symm p.1, p.2)) := by
  have hP : ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) ∞
      (Prod.map f.symm (id : unitInterval → unitInterval)) :=
    f.symm.contMDiff.prodMap contMDiff_id
  refine ⟨hF.1.comp hP, fun p v ↦ ?_⟩
  -- The motion of the conjugate is `f ∘ Φ ∘ (f⁻¹ × id)`, and `f⁻¹ × id` sends `∂ₜ` to `∂ₜ`
  -- and `(v, 0)` to `(df⁻¹ v, 0)`.
  have hdP (w : TangentSpace (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) p) :
      mfderiv (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) (Prod.map f.symm (id : unitInterval → unitInterval))
        p w = (mfderiv J J f.symm p.1 w.1, w.2) := by
    have := Manifold.mfderiv_prodMap_apply (f.symm.mdifferentiable (by simp) p.1)
      (mdifferentiableAt_id (I := 𝓡∂ 1) (x := p.2)) (w.1, w.2)
    rw [Manifold.tangentSpaceProdEquiv_symm_apply, Manifold.tangentSpaceProdEquiv_symm_apply,
      mfderiv_id, ContinuousLinearMap.id_apply] at this
    -- `(w.1, w.2)` is `w` by eta for pairs.
    exact this
  rw [cylinderMap_transDiffeomorph, ← Function.comp_assoc,
    mpullback_comp (hP.mdifferentiable (by simp))
      ((f.contMDiff.comp Φ.contMDiff_cylinderMap).mdifferentiable (by simp)),
    mpullback_comp (Φ.contMDiff_cylinderMap.mdifferentiable (by simp))
      (f.mdifferentiable (by simp)), ← SmoothForm.coe_mpullback f f.contMDiff σ, mpullback_apply]
  refine (congrArg _ (funext fun i : Fin 2 ↦ ?_)).trans
    (((hF.2 (f.symm p.1, p.2) (mfderiv J J f.symm p.1 v))).trans ?_)
  · fin_cases i
    · exact (hdP _).trans (Prod.ext (map_zero _) rfl)
    · exact hdP _
  · exact ((mvfderiv_comp_apply (g := F) p (hF.1.mdifferentiableAt (by simp))
      (hP.mdifferentiableAt (by simp)) ((v, 0) : TangentSpace (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) p)).trans
        (congrArg _ (hdP _))).symm

/-- A diffeotopy `φ_t` is **Hamiltonian** for a two-form `σ` when every map `φ_t` preserves `σ`
and `φ_t` has a Hamiltonian read along its motion (`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian`): it is
generated by a smooth time-dependent Hamiltonian `H_t`, `ι_{X_t} σ = dH_t`. For a closed `σ` these
are the smooth Hamiltonian isotopies of `(M, σ)` starting at the identity. -/
def IsHamiltonian (σ : SmoothForm J M ℝ 2) (Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M) : Prop :=
  (∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) ∧ ∃ F, Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F

/-- Unfolding `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsHamiltonian`: every `φ_t` preserves `σ` and `φ_t` has a
Hamiltonian, read along its motion. -/
theorem isHamiltonian_iff : Φ.IsHamiltonian σ ↔
    (∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) ∧ ∃ F, Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- Every map `φ_t` of a Hamiltonian diffeotopy preserves `σ`. -/
theorem IsHamiltonian.timeSlice_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer (hΦ : Φ.IsHamiltonian σ)
    (t : unitInterval) : Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ :=
  hΦ.1 t

/-- A Hamiltonian diffeotopy has a Hamiltonian, read along its motion. -/
theorem IsHamiltonian.exists_hasHamiltonian (hΦ : Φ.IsHamiltonian σ) :
    ∃ F, Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F :=
  hΦ.2

/-- The constant diffeotopy is Hamiltonian. -/
theorem isHamiltonian_refl : (refl J ∞ M).IsHamiltonian σ :=
  ⟨SmoothForm.timeSlice_refl_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer, 0, hasHamiltonian_refl⟩

/-- The pointwise composite `ψ_t ∘ φ_t` of Hamiltonian diffeotopies is Hamiltonian. -/
theorem IsHamiltonian.trans (hΦ : Φ.IsHamiltonian σ) (hΨ : Ψ.IsHamiltonian σ) :
    (Φ.trans Ψ).IsHamiltonian σ := by
  obtain ⟨hΦσ, F, hF⟩ := hΦ
  obtain ⟨hΨσ, G, hG⟩ := hΨ
  exact ⟨SmoothForm.timeSlice_trans_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer hΦσ hΨσ, _, hF.trans hG hΨσ⟩

/-- The pointwise inverse `φ_t⁻¹` of a Hamiltonian diffeotopy is Hamiltonian. -/
theorem IsHamiltonian.symm (hΦ : Φ.IsHamiltonian σ) : Φ.symm.IsHamiltonian σ := by
  obtain ⟨hΦσ, F, hF⟩ := hΦ
  exact ⟨SmoothForm.timeSlice_symm_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer hΦσ, _, hF.symm hΦσ⟩

/-- Conjugating a Hamiltonian diffeotopy `φ_t` by a diffeomorphism `f` preserving `σ` gives the
Hamiltonian diffeotopy `f ∘ φ_t ∘ f⁻¹`. -/
theorem IsHamiltonian.transDiffeomorph {f : M ≃ₘ⟮J, J⟯ M}
    (hf : f ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) (hΦ : Φ.IsHamiltonian σ) :
    (Φ.transDiffeomorph f).IsHamiltonian σ := by
  obtain ⟨hΦσ, F, hF⟩ := hΦ
  refine ⟨SmoothForm.timeSlice_transDiffeomorph_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer hf hΦσ,
    fun p ↦ F (f.symm p.1, p.2), HasHamiltonian.transDiffeomorph (F := F) f ?_⟩
  rwa [SmoothForm.mem_diffeomorphStabilizer.1 hf]

/-- The flux form of a Hamiltonian diffeotopy is exact. -/
theorem IsHamiltonian.fluxForm_mem_exactForms (hΦ : Φ.IsHamiltonian σ) :
    Φ.fluxForm σ ∈ exactForms J M 1 :=
  hΦ.2.choose_spec.fluxForm_mem_exactForms

/-- **The flux of a Hamiltonian isotopy vanishes.** -/
theorem IsHamiltonian.flux_eq_zero {σ : closedForms J M 2} (hΦ : Φ.IsHamiltonian σ.val)
    (h : Φ.final ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ.val) : Φ.flux σ h = 0 :=
  hΦ.2.choose_spec.flux_eq_zero h

/-! ### Autonomous Hamiltonian flows -/

section Flow

variable [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [J.Boundaryless] [T2Space M] {σ : SmoothTwoForm J M}
  {X : Cₛ^∞⟮J; E, TangentSpace J (M := M)⟯} {f : M → ℝ}

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [J.Boundaryless] [T2Space M] in
/-- A Hamiltonian vector field of a smooth function `f` is symplectic: the existing
`SmoothTwoForm.mem_symplecticVectorFields_of_isHamiltonianVectorField`, applied to the smooth
zero-form `f`. -/
private theorem mem_symplecticVectorFields_of_isHamiltonianVectorField_of_contMDiff
    (hf : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ f) (hX : σ.IsHamiltonianVectorField f X) :
    X ∈ σ.symplecticVectorFields :=
  SmoothTwoForm.mem_symplecticVectorFields_of_isHamiltonianVectorField
    (φ := ⟨RoughForm.ofFunction J f, (isSmoothForm_ofFunction_iff.2 hf).mem_smoothBundleForms⟩)
    (by simpa only [RoughForm.ofFunction_apply] using hX)

/-- **Autonomous Hamiltonian flows are Hamiltonian diffeotopies.** For a complete Hamiltonian
vector field `X` of a smooth function `f`, `ι_X σ = df`, the diffeotopy which runs the flow of `X`
for duration `a` has the Hamiltonian `(x, t) ↦ a f(x)`, read along its motion. -/
theorem hasHamiltonian_globalFlowDiffeotopy (hf : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ f)
    (hX : σ.IsHamiltonianVectorField f X) (hc : IsCompleteVectorField X) (a : ℝ) :
    (globalFlowDiffeotopy le_top X.contMDiff hc a).HasHamiltonian σ (fun p ↦ a * f p.1) := by
  have hXi : RoughForm.interior X σ.val = mextDeriv (RoughForm.ofFunction J f) :=
    SmoothTwoForm.isHamiltonianVectorField_iff_interior_eq.1 hX
  have hXs := mem_symplecticVectorFields_of_isHamiltonianVectorField_of_contMDiff hf hX
  have hfst : ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ (f ∘ Prod.fst : M × unitInterval → ℝ) :=
    hf.comp contMDiff_fst
  have hF : ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ (fun p : M × unitInterval ↦ a * f p.1) :=
    (contDiff_const.mul contDiff_id).contMDiff.comp hfst
  refine ⟨hF, fun p v ↦ ?_⟩
  -- The motion `(x, t) ↦ ψ_(a t) x` has velocity `a X` and spatial derivative `dψ_(a t)`, and the
  -- flow preserves `ι_X σ = df`.
  have hpull : mpullback (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) J
      (globalFlowDiffeotopy le_top X.contMDiff hc a).cylinderMap σ.val p
        ![((0 : E), (1 : TangentSpace (𝓡∂ 1) p.2)), (v, (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))] =
      σ.val (flowOf X (a * p.2) p.1) (Matrix.vecCons (a • X (flowOf X (a * p.2) p.1))
        fun i ↦ mfderiv J J (flowOf X (a * p.2)) p.1 (![v] i)) := by
    refine (mpullback_apply _ _ _ _).trans ?_
    rw [congrFun (cylinderMap_globalFlowDiffeotopy le_top X.contMDiff hc a) p]
    refine congrArg _ (funext fun i : Fin 2 ↦ ?_)
    fin_cases i
    · exact mfderiv_cylinderMap_globalFlowDiffeotopy_time le_top X.contMDiff hc a p
    · exact mfderiv_cylinderMap_globalFlowDiffeotopy_space le_top X.contMDiff hc a p v
  refine (hpull.trans (apply_vecCons_smul_mfderiv_flowOf hXs hc a (a * p.2) p.1 ![v])).trans ?_
  rw [SmoothTwoForm.coe_interiorₗ, hXi]
  refine (congrArg (a • ·) (mextDeriv_ofFunction_apply f p.1 v)).trans ?_
  -- The derivative of `(x, t) ↦ a f(x)` along `(v, 0)` is `a df(v)`.
  have hd := DFunLike.congr_fun (const_smul_mfderiv (z := p) (hfst.mdifferentiableAt (by simp)) a)
    ((v, 0) : TangentSpace (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) p)
  exact (congrArg (a • ·)
    (mvfderiv_comp_fst_apply f p ((v, 0) : TangentSpace (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) p)).symm).trans hd.symm

/-- For a closed two-form `σ`, the flow of a complete Hamiltonian vector field `X` of a smooth
function, run for duration `a`, is a Hamiltonian diffeotopy. -/
theorem isHamiltonian_globalFlowDiffeotopy (hσ : σ.IsClosed) (hf : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ f)
    (hX : σ.IsHamiltonianVectorField f X) (hc : IsCompleteVectorField X) (a : ℝ) :
    (globalFlowDiffeotopy le_top X.contMDiff hc a).IsHamiltonian σ :=
  ⟨timeSlice_globalFlowDiffeotopy_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer hσ
    (mem_symplecticVectorFields_of_isHamiltonianVectorField_of_contMDiff hf hX) hc a, _,
    hasHamiltonian_globalFlowDiffeotopy hf hX hc a⟩

end Flow

end Diffeotopy

namespace SmoothForm

variable {E H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace H]
  {J : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H} {M : Type*} [TopologicalSpace M] [ChartedSpace H M]
  [IsManifold J ∞ M] {σ : SmoothForm J M ℝ 2}

/-! ### The Hamiltonian group -/

variable (σ) in
/-- The **Hamiltonian group** `Ham(M, σ)` of a two-form `σ`: the final diffeomorphisms `φ₁` of the
Hamiltonian diffeotopies `φ_t` of `σ` (`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsHamiltonian`). For a symplectic form
these are the time-one maps of smooth time-dependent Hamiltonian flows. -/
def hamiltonianGroup : Subgroup (M ≃ₘ⟮J, J⟯ M) where
  carrier := {φ | ∃ Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M, Φ.IsHamiltonian σ ∧ Φ.final = φ}
  one_mem' := ⟨Diffeotopy.refl J ∞ M, Diffeotopy.isHamiltonian_refl, Diffeotopy.final_refl⟩
  mul_mem' := by
    rintro _ _ ⟨Φ, hΦ, rfl⟩ ⟨Ψ, hΨ, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨Ψ.trans Φ, hΨ.trans hΦ, by rw [Diffeotopy.final_trans, Diffeomorph.mul_def]⟩
  inv_mem' := by
    rintro _ ⟨Φ, hΦ, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨Φ.symm, hΦ.symm, by rw [Diffeotopy.final_symm, Diffeomorph.inv_def]⟩

/-- A diffeomorphism lies in the Hamiltonian group of `σ` exactly when it is the final
diffeomorphism of a Hamiltonian diffeotopy. -/
theorem mem_hamiltonianGroup {φ : M ≃ₘ⟮J, J⟯ M} :
    φ ∈ hamiltonianGroup σ ↔ ∃ Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M, Φ.IsHamiltonian σ ∧ Φ.final = φ :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- The final diffeomorphism of a Hamiltonian diffeotopy lies in the Hamiltonian group. -/
theorem final_mem_hamiltonianGroup {Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M} (hΦ : Φ.IsHamiltonian σ) :
    Φ.final ∈ hamiltonianGroup σ :=
  ⟨Φ, hΦ, rfl⟩

/-- Hamiltonian diffeomorphisms are isotopic to the identity through diffeomorphisms preserving
`σ`. -/
theorem hamiltonianGroup_le_isotopyStabilizer : hamiltonianGroup σ ≤ isotopyStabilizer σ := by
  rintro _ ⟨Φ, hΦ, rfl⟩
  exact final_mem_isotopyStabilizer hΦ.1

/-- Conjugating a Hamiltonian diffeomorphism by a diffeomorphism `f` preserving `σ` gives a
Hamiltonian diffeomorphism. -/
theorem mul_mul_inv_mem_hamiltonianGroup {f φ : M ≃ₘ⟮J, J⟯ M}
    (hf : f ∈ diffeomorphStabilizer σ) (hφ : φ ∈ hamiltonianGroup σ) :
    f * φ * f⁻¹ ∈ hamiltonianGroup σ := by
  obtain ⟨Φ, hΦ, rfl⟩ := hφ
  exact ⟨Φ.transDiffeomorph f, hΦ.transDiffeomorph hf,
    Diffeotopy.final_transDiffeomorph_eq_mul_mul_inv Φ f⟩

/-- The Hamiltonian group of `σ` is a normal subgroup of the group of diffeomorphisms preserving
`σ`. -/
instance normal_hamiltonianGroup_subgroupOf_diffeomorphStabilizer :
    ((hamiltonianGroup σ).subgroupOf (diffeomorphStabilizer σ)).Normal :=
  (Subgroup.normal_subgroupOf_iff
    (hamiltonianGroup_le_isotopyStabilizer.trans isotopyStabilizer_le_diffeomorphStabilizer)).2
    fun _ _ hφ hf ↦ mul_mul_inv_mem_hamiltonianGroup hf hφ

/-- The Hamiltonian group of `σ` is a normal subgroup of the isotopy stabilizer of `σ`. -/
instance normal_hamiltonianGroup_subgroupOf_isotopyStabilizer :
    ((hamiltonianGroup σ).subgroupOf (isotopyStabilizer σ)).Normal :=
  (Subgroup.normal_subgroupOf_iff hamiltonianGroup_le_isotopyStabilizer).2
    fun _ _ hφ hf ↦
      mul_mul_inv_mem_hamiltonianGroup (isotopyStabilizer_le_diffeomorphStabilizer hf) hφ

end SmoothForm

/-- **Hamiltonian diffeomorphisms have trivial endpoint flux.** For a closed two-form `σ`, the
Hamiltonian group lies in the kernel of the endpoint flux `G_σ → H¹_dR(M) / Γ_σ`. -/
theorem hamiltonianGroup_subgroupOf_le_ker_endpointFlux {E H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [NormedSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace H] {J : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H} {M : Type*}
    [TopologicalSpace M] [ChartedSpace H M] [IsManifold J ∞ M] (σ : closedForms J M 2) :
    (SmoothForm.hamiltonianGroup σ.val).subgroupOf (SmoothForm.isotopyStabilizer σ.val) ≤
      (endpointFlux σ).ker := by
  intro φ hφ
  obtain ⟨Φ, hΦ, hfin⟩ := SmoothForm.mem_hamiltonianGroup.1 (Subgroup.mem_subgroupOf.1 hφ)
  exact mem_ker_endpointFlux_iff.2 ⟨Φ, hΦ.1, hfin, hΦ.flux_eq_zero _⟩

end TauCeti
